{"run_id":"demo-po1003-granite","seq":17,"ts":"2026-10-24T11:14:43Z","type":"baseline","payload":{"chunks":[{"id":"https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SOP-002-s4","cls":"Chunk","label":"SOP-002 §ST02_SEALING TMP thresholds","description":null,"text":"ST02_SEALING TMP: °C 165.0 175.0 185.0 ± 1.2 195.0 210.0 E-STOP ST02/ST03/ST04; inspect element","props":{"page":1},"score":0.7282},{"id":"https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SOP-001-s3","cls":"Chunk","label":"SOP-001 §2.2 ST02_SEALING","description":null,"text":"2.2 ST02_SEALING RULE-ST02-01: TMP MUST remain between 175°C and 195°C. RULE-ST02-02: TMP > 210°C (CRITICAL) — emergency stop ST02, ST03, ST04. RULE-ST02-03: CUR increase >1.5 A above nominal sustained >5 min — schedule maintenance. RULE-ST02-04: CUR drift at ST02_SEALING CORRELATES with speed reduction at ST04_PACKAGING due to shared electrical coupling. Monitor ST04_PACKAGING-SPD whenever ST02_SEALING-CUR triggers a WARNING.","props":{"page":1},"score":0.7225},{"id":"https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/SOP-003-s6","cls":"Chunk","label":"SOP-003 §MAINT-06","description":null,"text":"MAINT-06 TMP WRH01_WAREHOUSE TMP DRIFT >2°C over 2 h Inspect compressor; notify QC CRITICAL","props":{"page":1},"score":0.7025}],"answer":"![SOP-002 §ST02_SEALING TMP thresholds](https://example.com/sop002_st02_sealing_tmp.png)\n\nThe sealing station can run at the temperature limit of 195°C, as SOP-001 §2.2 states that the temperature must remain between 175°C and 195°C. SOP-003 §MAINT-06 does not mention the sealing station, so it does not provide information about who supplies the temperature sensor for the sealing station.","illustrative":false}}
